second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Which person or organization did Claire Rogers work for?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 13, \"text\": \"Claire Rogers\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 15, \"end\": 106, \"text\": \"Claire Rogers is a researcher who has made significant contributions to her field of study.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 107, \"end\": 262, \"text\": \"One notable aspect of her career is her association with Curtin University, a prominent institution of higher learning located in Perth, Western Australia.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 263, \"end\": 290, \"text\": \"Career at Curtin University\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 292, \"end\": 410, \"text\": \"Claire Rogers worked as a researcher at Curtin University, where she was involved in various projects and initiatives.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 411, \"end\": 569, \"text\": \"According to her profile on ResearchGate, a social networking site for scientists and researchers, Rogers listed Curtin University as one of her affiliations.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 570, \"end\": 677, \"text\": \"[1] This suggests that she was actively engaged with the university's research community during her tenure.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 678, \"end\": 813, \"text\": \"Furthermore, a search of Curtin University's staff directory archives reveals that Claire Rogers was indeed employed by the university.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 814, \"end\": 961, \"text\": \"Although the exact dates of her employment are not publicly available, her presence in the directory confirms her association with the institution.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 962, \"end\": 965, \"text\": \"[2]\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 967, \"end\": 1131, \"text\": \"Rogers' research focus and expertise align with Curtin University's strengths in various fields, including science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM).\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1132, \"end\": 1252, \"text\": \"Her work has likely contributed to the university's reputation as a hub for innovative research and academic excellence.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1253, \"end\": 1264, \"text\": \"References:\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1266, \"end\": 1283, \"text\": \"[1] ResearchGate.\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1284, \"end\": 1291, \"text\": \"(n.d.).\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1292, \"end\": 1306, \"text\": \"Claire Rogers.\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1307, \"end\": 1378, \"text\": \"Retrieved from <https:\\\\/\\\\/www.researchgate.net\\\\/profile\\\\/Claire_Rogers>\"}, \"D1S18\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1380, \"end\": 1402, \"text\": \"[2] Curtin University.\"}, \"D1S19\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1403, \"end\": 1410, \"text\": \"(n.d.).\"}, \"D1S20\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1411, \"end\": 1427, \"text\": \"Staff Directory.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 205, \"text\": \"As Claire Rogers navigated the labyrinthine corridors of the BGI Genomics headquarters in Shenzhen, the soft hum of sequencers and the gentle chatter of her colleagues created a soothing background melody.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 206, \"end\": 373, \"text\": \"It was a typical Wednesday morning, with the aroma of freshly brewed coffee wafting from the break room, enticing her to grab a cup before diving into the day's tasks.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 374, \"end\": 515, \"text\": \"Claire, a renowned geneticist, had been with BGI for nearly five years, and the company's cutting-edge facilities had become her second home.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 516, \"end\": 698, \"text\": \"As she settled into her workstation, surrounded by rows of sleek, silver machines, Claire's mind began to wander back to the project that had brought her to China in the first place.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 699, \"end\": 839, \"text\": \"The ambitious \\\"Genome of the People\\\" initiative, aimed at mapping the genetic diversity of the world's populations, had been her brainchild.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 840, \"end\": 928, \"text\": \"BGI's resources and expertise had been the perfect catalyst to bring her vision to life.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 929, \"end\": 1078, \"text\": \"Claire's gaze drifted to the framed photograph on her desk, showing her alongside BGI's charismatic CEO, Wang Jian, at the project's launch ceremony.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1079, \"end\": 1234, \"text\": \"The memory of his words still resonated with her: \\\"Together, we will unlock the secrets of humanity's genetic code and pave the way for a brighter future.\\\"\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1235, \"end\": 1413, \"text\": \"It was a sentiment that had drawn her to BGI in the first place – the company's commitment to pushing the boundaries of genetic research and its potential to improve human lives.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1414, \"end\": 1543, \"text\": \"As she began to analyze the latest batch of genomic data, Claire's thoughts were interrupted by the arrival of her colleague, Dr.\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1544, \"end\": 1551, \"text\": \"Li Wei.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1552, \"end\": 1626, \"text\": \"\\\"Claire, have you seen the latest updates on the Tibetan Plateau samples?\\\"\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1627, \"end\": 1672, \"text\": \"he asked, his eyes sparkling with excitement.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1673, \"end\": 1838, \"text\": \"Claire's mind snapped back into focus, and she leaned in, eager to discuss the intriguing patterns they had begun to uncover in the region's unique genetic heritage.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1839, \"end\": 1957, \"text\": \"In this moment, surrounded by the trappings of BGI's state-of-the-art facility, Claire felt a deep sense of belonging.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1958, \"end\": 2125, \"text\": \"She was exactly where she was meant to be – at the forefront of genetic research, driven by her passion for discovery and her commitment to the betterment of humanity.\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2126, \"end\": 2311, \"text\": \"The soft glow of the sequencers, the hum of the machines, and the quiet intensity of her colleagues all blended together to create an atmosphere that was both familiar and exhilarating.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"Claire Rogers\", \"scope\": \"organization\", \"claim\": \"Claire Rogers worked for BGI Genomics.\", \"answer\": \"BGI Genomics\", \"quote\": \"As Claire Rogers navigated the labyrinthine corridors of the BGI Genomics headquarters in Shenzhen, the soft hum of sequencers and the gentle chatter of her colleagues created a soothing background melody. It was a typical Wednesday morning, with the aroma of freshly brewed coffee wafting from the break room, enticing her to grab a cup before diving into the day's tasks. Claire, a renowned geneticist, had been with BGI for nearly five years, and the company's cutting-edge facilities had become her second home. As she settled into her workstation, surrounded by rows of sleek, silver machines, Claire's mind began to wander back to the project that had brought her to China in the first place. The ambitious \\\"Genome of the People\\\" initiative, aimed at mapping the genetic diversity of the world's populations, had been her brainchild. BGI's resources and expertise had been the perfect catalyst to bring her vision to life. Claire's gaze drifted to the framed photograph on her desk, showing her alongside BGI's charismatic CEO, Wang Jian, at the project's launch ceremony.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Curtin University\", \"BGI Genomics\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Curtin University\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"BGI Genomics\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
